cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "Detectability benchmark: survey-planning questions for language models, with physics-based reference answers"
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  Fifty realistic near-surface survey-planning scenarios (karst, mine workings, tunnels, archaeology, geology and ore,
  ferrous objects and unexploded ordnance), each based on a published case study or survey guidance, with its sources,
  assumptions and a natural-language question. Reference answers for gravity, total-field magnetic and magnetic
  gradiometer surveys are computed with Detectability 0.3.0. A pilot run scores Claude Opus 5.5 with and without the
  Detectability tool.
